## Set up

Payments › Packages and settings walks you through three steps: connect Stripe (Stripe's own sign-up,
about 10 minutes), make a package, and put it on an invite link. You're the seller: your own VAT and
refunds, all in Stripe. Stripe's card fees are yours; LogIt takes nothing.

People who open a paid link see your package and price first. If they're new to LogIt they make an
account right on that page, then pay on Stripe's page, where they can also type a discount code you
made under Coupons in your Stripe dashboard. You get an email when someone pays.

## When a payment fails

LogIt emails the client a link to update their card, and Stripe tries the card again over a few days.
Clients can also press Update card in My coach on the web; Stripe takes the overdue payment as soon as the
new card is in. You choose what happens to coaching meanwhile, for everyone or per client, and you get an
email too (turn these off in Packages and settings).

